  "attestation": "D-133 closed-loop round 2 fixes on needs-wording (audit of 6c159a3: 3 HIGH, 6 MEDIUM, 4 LOW), held to two principles across every kind. P1 (narrow, fail-safe mechanism change in alembic_needs.mjs apply): a correction is kept only on an exact Keep and undone only on an exact Undo, an approval only on an exact Approve or Not yet; any other answer is skipped and asked again, never silently kept (before, any correction answer other than Undo was kept); digest answers are read exactly as before (removing choices never changes how answerDigest reads an answer); interrupts record any answer as the answer. HIGH-B: a correction always offers Keep/Undo; when before/after cannot be shown the detail says the page holds the corrected passage exactly as Keep leaves it. P2: an answer that confirms or adopts what units hold (Confirm on exercise data or a stale confirmation, Keep as written, Accept as mine, Keep on an unasked edit) shows each whole unit text; when one cannot be shown or read, no one-click choice and the question says the page holds the exact text (HIGH-C, MEDIUM-D, MEDIUM-L); a reviewer suggestion and a removed passage, on no page, are always shown in full (MEDIUM-E); applying a suggestion and accept as mine are never pre-chosen, and the recommendation line is kept whenever it says more than the choice (MEDIUM-F). HIGH-A: accents become combining marks (x bar, H hat, F vec, nu tilde, A ring as the angstrom sign), menclose stays visible (struck, boxed, circled). MEDIUM-G and LOW-I: orz-markdown MAX_TEX and TEX_DEFINES mirrored (not exported); such a formula, or one KaTeX rejects, reads as its source; KaTeX version checked against orz-markdown KATEX_VERSION. MEDIUM-H: decision codes are removed only from harness notes; an assessment-guide entry title is rendered, not passed through the harness pass. LOW-J: arrow conditions top first; binomial without double parentheses. LOW-K: assistant units capped at 20 with a count. LOW-M: orz-markdown dollar rule in light text; in agent words only a path with a folder reads as a page. Probes adopted as tests/needs-wording.audit2.test.mjs (HIGH-B adapted to the fix asked for: Keep/Undo always offered; it checks a non-choice undo is not kept, and that a record from a hand-in without choices keeps only on an exact Keep), registered as evidence of req.host.alembic-needs-wording and req.host.alembic-needs-apply, both statements updated. Earlier tests updated for P2 (a confirmation of a passage the context cannot read offers no choice) and agent words keeping codes. CHANGELOG Unreleased states the mechanism change plainly; VERSION unchanged. Reviewed every required item. Tests: the 36 required plus alembic-needs, alembic-needs-wording, needs-wording.audit, needs-wording.audit2 and job-release: 598 passed, 0 failed (COURSEWERK_FRAMES=installed, concurrency 2, one test process under the shared lock).",
